$NetBSD$

\w is a GNU sed extension.  BSD sed reads the backslash as trailing
and fails, so make-support/find-tests.gmk is never generated:

  sed: 1: "s/\\([^ ]*\\)\\w*=.*/\\1/gp": RE error: trailing backslash (\\)

The build carries on -- the target is not fatal -- but the cache never
settles and make test has no groups to work from.  [[:alnum:]_] is what
\w stands for and is in POSIX, so every sed agrees on it.

Still present in openjdk/jdk25u at master, so this is not waiting on a
rebase.

--- make/common/FindTests.gmk.orig
+++ make/common/FindTests.gmk
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 	( $(foreach root, $(JTREG_TESTROOTS), \
 	    $(ECHO) ""; \
 	    $(PRINTF) "\n%s_JTREG_TEST_GROUPS := " "$(root)"; \
-	    $(SED) -n -e 's/^\#.*//g' -e 's/\([^ ]*\)\w*=.*/\1/gp' \
+	    $(SED) -n -e 's/^\#.*//g' -e 's/\([^ ]*\)[[:alnum:]_]*=.*/\1/gp' \
 	      $($(root)_JTREG_GROUP_FILES) \
 	      | $(SORT) -u | $(TR) '\n' ' ' ; \
 	  ) \
